 V('Declaration of Conscience=Declaração de Consciência|first woman elected to both houses=primeira mulher eleita para as duas casas|Senate floor speech=discurso no plenário do Senado|political courage=coragem política|right to dissent=direito de discordar|even-handed treatment=tratamento equânime|guilt by accusation=culpa por acusação|McCarthy-era tactics=táticas da era McCarthy|Cold War climate=clima da Guerra Fria|loyalty fears=temor de deslealdade|free speech defence=defesa da liberdade de expressão|civil liberties=liberdades civis|moderate Republican=republicana moderada|Maine politics=política do Maine|small-town beginnings=origens em cidade pequena|House seat=cadeira na Câmara|Senate career=carreira no Senado|presidential nomination bid=disputa pela indicação presidencial|principled stand=posição de princípio|cost of dissent=custo da dissidência|lost allies=aliados perdidos|ethical standing=autoridade ética|official archive=arquivo oficial|historical memory=memória histórica|scholarly assessment=avaliação acadêmica|archive collection=acervo de arquivo|biography chapter=capítulo de biografia|commemorative plaque=placa comemorativa|statesmanship=habilidade de estadista|legislative service=serviço legislativo'),
 ('Civics class',[('Teacher','Why is the 1950 speech remembered?','Por que o discurso de 1950 é lembrado?'),('Student','Because she defended dissent without naming McCarthy.','Porque defendeu a divergência sem nomear McCarthy.'),('Teacher','Did it cost her anything?','Custou-lhe algo?'),('Student','Some allies, but it is seen as courageous.','Alguns aliados, mas é visto como corajoso.')]),
 [('Summarise her career.','Resuma.','She rose from local politics to the U.S. Senate.'),('Use without + -ing.','Use.','She criticised the tactics without naming the senator.'),('Use cost.','Use.','The speech cost her some allies.')],
 ('Write a 6-sentence biography of a political or civic figure who spoke out at a crucial moment (real, with safe facts, or fictional).','Dr. Elena Voss, a fictional city health officer, warned in 1998 that the water supply was unsafe. She spoke at a council meeting without notes, naming the evidence rather than the officials. The warning cost her a promotion. Yet it is widely remembered as the moment that forced reform. She continued to serve until retirement. Her speech is still quoted in public-health courses.',['Usei **participial**','Usei **cost**','Usei **widely remembered**'],'6 frases'),
