 [('Read the first four lines aloud.','Leia.','It weighs no more than a leaf, this slip of paper in my hand.'),('Explain the contrast of scale.','Explique.','A tiny paper stands for the whole nation.'),('Identify a metaphor.','Identifique.','The queue is a river.')],
 ('Write an 8-line poem or free verse about a civic act (voting, volunteering, marching), using one metaphor and one contrast of scale.','A lantern, small as a thumb, / is carried to the square. / Behind it, a thousand more, / each one a quiet vow. / Alone, a spark; together, a street / that will not be dark again. / What is a march but this: / the light that learns to walk?',['Usei **metáfora**','Usei **contraste de escala**'],'6–8 linhas'),
